  "historical_output_text": " I just realized the handle for a few kitchen drawers and my microwave are completely detached and now everything spills all of them when opening, can anyone recommend some fixes?\nAbsolutely I get you! That sounds frustrating and messy.\n\nOne easy DIY repair solution for kitchen handle detachers (assuming the handle isn'y just a loose attachment) would probably be replacing the hardware itself, which is often readily accessible online at hardware or big home goods store, as it can sometimes wear or come off from years and repeated opening. Look up a guide specific for your kitchen drawer type as replacement procedures might slightly alter based. Make a list and compare costs online to make a smart buying call and purchase all new needed handles. If your handle has completely fallen, you can sometimes get by just screw driving off the back and reinsert a replacement one, if available and not completely damaged.\n\nIf",
